meta {
  name: negative bind wrong enrollmentId type
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/enrollments/bind
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
      "enrollmentId": "not-an-integer",
      "enrollmentProofToken": "schema-validation-probe"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  test("Status is 4xx (schema or request validation)", function () {
      expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.at.least(400);
      expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.below(500);
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Deliberately invalid Auth bind body: `enrollmentId` is a string, but the OpenAPI schema
  requires `integer` (`int32`). The mobile app cannot produce this request.

  **Use with environment `exp1`.** On EXP1 Cloudflare schema validation **Block**, expect HTTP
  **403** Error **1020** (API Shield / WAF). Bruno sends `Accept` JSON, so the body is Cloudflare's
  RFC 9457 JSON (`cloudflare_error: true`, `error_code: 1020`, `ray_id`, `type` under
  `developers.cloudflare.com`), not an Ezkey `https://ezkey.io/problems/…` ProblemDetail.

  A Spring ProblemDetail (`type` under `https://ezkey.io/problems/`, often HTTP 400) means the
  request **reached origin** — not schema-Block evidence. Against **local**, Jackson/Bean
  Validation also returns 4xx; that is not a Cloudflare check.

  Extra undeclared properties are a weak probe: `EnrollmentBindRequestDto` does not set
  `additionalProperties: false`, so Cloudflare may accept them.

  **Do not add this request to `bruno-health.sh` suites.** Operator reading:
  `docs/cloudflare/auth-api-schema-validation.md` § Reading responses.
}
